What the three Go platforms emit for a method on a user type that touches a
package var, and how the Model reaches it.

A type method is lifted to a free function, and the Model arrives as a
**trailing parameter**: the receiver slot is already spent on the value.

`doubled` and `viaCalc` are the two transitive legs, and neither touches a var
of its own: a method reaching one through a method, and a top-level func
reaching one through a method.

`plain` is the control. It touches nothing, so it stays the two-argument free
function it was, and the `CalcPlain` deny below is what says so if the
predicate ever widens to every type method. It recurses because passInlinePure
substitutes a pure one away otherwise, and a golden with no plain lifted method
in it would leave that deny asserting nothing.

Note the spelling of the argument differs by platform and must. bubbletea's
hand-written receivers are `func (m Model)` -- Update mutates the copy and
hands it back -- so a call from one of those passes `&m`, which is what the
click handler is here to show, a bubbletea handler body being emitted into
Update; fyne and gtk4 hold a `*Model` throughout and pass `m`.

deny * `(?m)^func CalcPending\(k Calc\) int` -- the lifted form takes the Model; without it the body names an undefined m
deny * `(?m)^func CalcDoubled\(k Calc\) int` -- a method reaching a var through a method takes it too
deny * `(?m)^func ViaCalc\(k Calc\) int` -- and so does a top-level func reaching one through a method
deny * `CalcPlain\(k Calc, n int, m \*Model\)` -- a method that touches no package var takes no Model, whatever else its type's methods do

-- app.sngl --
import . "sngl:ui"

output {
    go {
        bubbletea
        fyne
        gtk4
    }
}

var log string = ""

struct Calc {
    base int
}

func Calc.pending(k Calc) int {
    log = log + "!"
    return k.base * 2
}

func Calc.doubled(k Calc) => k.pending() * 2

func viaCalc(k Calc) => k.doubled() + 1

func Calc.plain(k Calc, n int) int {
    if n <= 0 {
        return k.base
    }
    return k.plain(n - 1)
}

component main node {
    var calc Calc = {base=3}
    var n int = 4
    var out = 0

    button(text="go", @click {
        out = calc.pending() + viaCalc(calc)
    })
    text(value="{out}{calc.plain(n)}")
}

window {
    main
}
